// Linux x86-64 syscall numbers (arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl).
//
// Every name is the kernel's syscall name in upper case and has type uint64, so
// it can be passed directly as the number argument of std::os::syscall0 through
// syscall6: std::os::syscall1(std::syscall::CLOSE, fd_word). Numbers 335-423 are
// unassigned on x86-64; 424 onward is shared by all architectures. Entries for
// removed or never-implemented syscalls (e.g. CREATE_MODULE, TUXCALL) remain
// for completeness and return ENOSYS. Prefer std::os typed wrappers when they exist.

